the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Jahreseinkommen of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    Härtefall anerkennen holds for *a case*.
    Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for *a case*.
    Begründung plausibel holds for *a case*.
    Einkommensgrenze unterschritten would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    Begründung plausibel is judged to hold for *a case*; open textured.

the knowledge base r4_11_hardship_case includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/hardship-case.ruml".

guidelines is published at "https://www.example.gov/haertefall-richtlinien.pdf".

Härtefall anerkennen holds for a case if
    Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for the case
    and Begründung plausibel holds for the case.

Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for a case if
    the Jahreseinkommen of the case is a number N
    and N < 25000.

% Where the expression has no result (a value it needs is missing), RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Jahreseinkommen of the case is a number
    and Einkommensgrenze unterschritten would hold for the case.

Begründung plausibel holds for a case if
    Begründung plausibel is judged to hold for the case.

scenario generated_1 is, as stated in "hardship-case.ruml" at generated_1:
    % every data point its first value
    the Jahreseinkommen of case 1 is 25000.
    node_1 expects answers [].
    not_node_1 expects answers ["it is not the case that Härtefall anerkennen holds for case 1"].
    node_2 expects answers [].
    not_node_2 expects answers ["it is not the case that Einkommensgrenze unterschritten holds for case 1"].
    node_3 expects answers ["Begründung plausibel holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.
    not_node_3 expects answers ["it is not the case that Begründung plausibel holds for case 1"] and any unknowns.

